{ daemon

  A thread has a (boolean) `daemon` property.
  -
  Setting this property to `True` marks the thread as a *daemon thread*. Daemon threads are intended to run in the background while non-daemon threads are active.
  -
  The process exits as soon as no non-daemon threads remain. Consequently, daemon threads may not have an opportunity to clean up their resources.

  The main (initial) thread does not have this property set.

  Demonstration program:
code {
import sys
import threading
import time


def work():
    time.sleep(10)
    print('Finished')


daemon = sys.argv[1].lower() == 'true' if len(sys.argv) > 1 else True

thread = threading.Thread(target=work)
thread.daemon = daemon
thread.start()

print(f'Main finished; daemon={daemon}')
